{"id":"0467963e96d3cbb8","group":"58","path":"58/batch06/58-df-zfc-cantor-scheme.md","title":"ZFC Cantor Scheme","display":"df-zfc-cantor-scheme — ZFC Cantor Scheme","type":"definition","metadata":{"type":"definition","book":"Set Theory","book_abbrev":"58","label":"58-df-zfc-cantor-scheme","aliases":["58-df-zfc-cantor-scheme"],"display":"df-zfc-cantor-scheme — ZFC Cantor Scheme","depends_on":["[[58-ax-zfc]]","[[58-df-cantor-space]]","[[58-df-function]]","[[58-df-powerset]]"]},"metadataError":null,"renderWarnings":[],"properties":[{"key":"type","html":"definition"},{"key":"book","html":"Set Theory"},{"key":"book_abbrev","html":"58"},{"key":"label","html":"58-df-zfc-cantor-scheme"},{"key":"aliases","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span>58-df-zfc-cantor-scheme</span></div>"},{"key":"display","html":"df-zfc-cantor-scheme — ZFC Cantor Scheme"},{"key":"depends_on","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-1\" data-note=\"a3348ed9eb6fb4e3\" href=\"?note=a3348ed9eb6fb4e3\" title=\"58-ax-zfc\">58-ax-zfc</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-2\" data-note=\"4e3b467d5761af40\" href=\"?note=4e3b467d5761af40\" title=\"58-df-cantor-space\">58-df-cantor-space</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-3\" data-note=\"36d7463d215be751\" href=\"?note=36d7463d215be751\" title=\"58-df-function\">58-df-function</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-4\" data-note=\"2b6b1d9eb78a2714\" href=\"?note=2b6b1d9eb78a2714\" title=\"58-df-powerset\">58-df-powerset</a></span></div>"}],"html":"\n<h2 id=\"Hypothesis\">[Hypothesis]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"S\">\\(S\\)</span> (ambient formal setting)</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathcal{U},X\\in V\">\\(\\mathcal{U},X\\in V\\)</span></li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{Function}\">\\(\\mathrm{Function}\\)</span> (function predicate, see <a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-5\" data-note=\"36d7463d215be751\" href=\"?note=36d7463d215be751\" title=\"58-df-function\">58-df-function</a>)</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{CantorScheme}_S:V^2\\to\\{\\top,\\bot\\}\">\\(\\mathrm{CantorScheme}_S:V^2\\to\\{\\top,\\bot\\}\\)</span> (predicate defined here)</li>\n</ul>\n<h2 id=\"Assertion\">[Assertion]</h2>\n<figure class=\"equation\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{df\\text{-}zfc\\text{-}cantor\\text{-}scheme} \\vdash \\mathrm{CantorScheme}_S(\\mathcal{U},X) \\leftrightarrow \\mathrm{Function}(\\mathcal U,2^{&lt;\\omega},\\mathcal P(X)\\setminus\\{\\emptyset\\})\\land \\forall s\\in2^{&lt;\\omega}\\;(\\mathcal{U}(s^\\frown 0)\\subseteq\\mathcal{U}(s)\\land \\mathcal{U}(s^\\frown 1)\\subseteq\\mathcal{U}(s)\\land \\mathcal{U}(s^\\frown 0)\\cap\\mathcal{U}(s^\\frown 1)=\\varnothing)\"><div class=\"math-display\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"数学公式\">\\[\\mathrm{df\\text{-}zfc\\text{-}cantor\\text{-}scheme} \\vdash \\mathrm{CantorScheme}_S(\\mathcal{U},X) \\leftrightarrow \\mathrm{Function}(\\mathcal U,2^{&lt;\\omega},\\mathcal P(X)\\setminus\\{\\emptyset\\})\\land \\forall s\\in2^{&lt;\\omega}\\;(\\mathcal{U}(s^\\frown 0)\\subseteq\\mathcal{U}(s)\\land \\mathcal{U}(s^\\frown 1)\\subseteq\\mathcal{U}(s)\\land \\mathcal{U}(s^\\frown 0)\\cap\\mathcal{U}(s^\\frown 1)=\\varnothing)\\]</div><button class=\"equation-action\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"展开查看完整公式\">展开公式 ↗</button></figure><h2 id=\"Remark\">[Remark]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathcal U\">\\(\\mathcal U\\)</span> is a total function on the finite binary sequences, every value is a nonempty subset of <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"X\">\\(X\\)</span>, and the two successor values are disjoint refinements of the parent value.</li>\n</ul>\n","headings":[{"id":"Hypothesis","text":"[Hypothesis]","level":2},{"id":"Assertion","text":"[Assertion]","level":2},{"id":"Remark","text":"[Remark]","level":2}],"links":[{"target":"58-ax-zfc","status":"resolved","id":"a3348ed9eb6fb4e3","anchor":